 A rendering method that ray-casts directly against a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) using distance fields to render isosurfaces, avoiding conversion to polygonal geometry. It uses a hybrid octree structure: an octree down to a certain level, then bricks of voxels for the final levels. Unlike [Sparse Voxel Octree Ray Tracing](2989-sparse-voxel-octree-ray-tracing.md) which may store down to individual voxel level, this method stores bricks of voxels at the bottom levels, which is more scalable for planetary scales and better suited for GPU application.
 
+### Full-screen SVO Raycasting
+Clears a raycasting leaf vector, loops over screen pixels, unprojects coordinates to view space, and casts rays against the octree [S10, unofficial]. Renders results by assigning colors based on Y components and drawing squares, while also rendering octree boxes with line polygon mode and color gradients based on scale [S10, unofficial].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: Depends on the depth of the tree and the number of nodes visited per ray. In the worst case (dense scene), it is proportional to the number of voxels; in sparse scenes, it is logarithmic with respect to the resolution [S10, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity**: Linear with respect to the number of nodes and leaves in the SVO. The implementation uses parallel arrays, requiring storage for node descriptors, child indices, and leaf data [S10, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity**: Not given in the sources. Typically logarithmic with respect to resolution for sparse scenes, linear for dense [G].
+*   **Memory Complexity**: Not given in the sources. Linear with respect to the number of nodes and leaves in the SVO [G].
 *   **Performance**: The provided implementation uses a GPU-side rendering phase with a single draw call for a fullscreen triangle, avoiding per-chunk draw calls [S8, unofficial]. Measured performance scales with traversal depth and hit density [S3, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths**: Efficient for sparse data; no need for dense texture memory; flexible resolution; enables real-time path tracing [S3, unofficial].
